# EtButton Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtButton` is a compositional button component for the eToro design system. It provides a flexible, accessible button with:

- **Multiple variants**: primary, info, negative colors with filled, subtle (more transparent bg), and ghost (text-only) styles
- **Multiple sizes**: tiny, small, medium, large
- **Compound component pattern**: `EtButton.Label` and `EtButton.Icon` subcomponents, or shorthand single string child
- **Built-in states**: loading, disabled
- **Haptic feedback**: enabled by default

**Does NOT handle:**

- Navigation logic (use with router/navigation handlers)
- Form submission logic (handle in parent)
- Icon-only buttons (use `EtIconButton` instead)
- Link-style buttons without padding (use `EtLink` instead)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtButton` (main component)

```tsx
<EtButton
  variant?: ButtonVariant    // default: 'primary-filled'
  size?: ButtonSize          // default: 'medium'
  disabled?: boolean         // default: false
  loading?: boolean          // default: false
  haptics?: boolean          // default: true
  stretch?: boolean          // default: false — full width of container
  forceColorScheme?: ButtonColorScheme  // pin colors to a fixed palette; ignores active theme
  onPress?: (event) => void
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  // ...other PressableProps
>
  {children}
</EtButton>
```

**Children constraints (enforced at runtime):**

- `string` - auto-wrapped in `EtButton.Label`
- `<EtButton.Label>` - text content
- `<EtButton.Icon>` - icon content
- Any other children will throw an error

### `EtButton.Label`

```tsx
<EtButton.Label
  variant?: TextVariant      // auto-sized based on button size
  style?: StyleProp<TextStyle>
  numberOfLines?: number     // default: 1
>
  {string}
</EtButton.Label>
```

### `EtButton.Icon`

```tsx
<EtButton.Icon
  name: IconName             // required - icon from icon library
  appearance?: {
    size?: number            // auto-sized based on button size
    color?: string           // auto-colored based on variant
  }
/>
```

### Types

| Type                | Values                                                                                                                                                                                    |
| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `ButtonVariant`     | `'primary-filled'` \| `'info-filled'` \| `'negative-filled'` \| `'primary-subtle'` \| `'info-subtle'` \| `'negative-subtle'` \| `'primary-ghost'` \| `'info-ghost'` \| `'negative-ghost'` |
| `ButtonSize`        | `'tiny'` \| `'small'` \| `'medium'` \| `'large'`                                                                                                                                          |
| `ButtonColorScheme` | `'light'` \| `'dark'`                                                                                                                                                                     |

## Usage Patterns

### String shorthand (simplest)

```tsx
<EtButton onPress={handlePress}>Click me</EtButton>
```

### Label with trailing icon

```tsx
<EtButton onPress={handlePress}>
  <EtButton.Label>Continue</EtButton.Label>
  <EtButton.Icon name="chevronRight" />
</EtButton>
```

### Icon with leading position (order matters!)

```tsx
<EtButton onPress={handlePress}>
  <EtButton.Icon name="plus" />
  <EtButton.Label>Add Item</EtButton.Label>
</EtButton>
```

### Negative/Destructive action

```tsx
<EtButton variant="negative-filled" onPress={handleDelete}>
  Delete Account
</EtButton>
```

### Loading state

```tsx
<EtButton loading={isSubmitting} onPress={handleSubmit}>
  Submit
</EtButton>
```

### Disabled state

```tsx
<EtButton disabled={!isValid} onPress={handleSubmit}>
  Submit
</EtButton>
```

### Pinned color scheme (theme-independent surfaces)

Use `forceColorScheme` when the button sits on a surface that always renders dark
(or light) regardless of the user's active theme — e.g. a dark promo card shown while
the app is in light mode. The whole button (background, label, icon, pressed states)
resolves from the fixed palette.

```tsx
// Always-dark upgrade CTA on a dark promo card, even in light mode
<EtButton variant="info-filled" size="small" forceColorScheme="dark" stretch onPress={goToPaywall}>
  Upgrade to Signature
</EtButton>
```

Prefer this over hand-rolling a `Pressable` + `Text` with frozen colors — it keeps
sizing, typography, pressed states, and accessibility consistent with the design system.

## Anti-patterns

### ❌ Passing arbitrary components as children

```tsx
// BAD - will throw runtime error
<EtButton>
  <View><Text>Custom content</Text></View>
</EtButton>

// BAD - don't use EtText directly, will throw runtime error
<EtButton>
  <EtText>Label</EtText>
</EtButton>
```

**Fix:** Use only `string`, `EtButton.Label`, or `EtButton.Icon` as children.

### ❌ Using EtButton for icon-only buttons

```tsx
// BAD - use EtIconButton instead
<EtButton>
  <EtButton.Icon name="close" />
</EtButton>
```

**Fix:** Use `EtIconButton` component for icon-only buttons.

### ❌ Manually styling colors/sizes

```tsx
// BAD - bypasses design system
<EtButton>
  <EtButton.Label style={{ color: 'red', fontSize: 20 }}>Text</EtButton.Label>
</EtButton>
```

**Fix:** Use `variant` prop to control appearance.

### ❌ Disabling haptics inconsistently

Only disable haptics when explicitly required (e.g., rapid-fire actions):

```tsx
// OK - rapid toggle doesn't need haptics
<EtButton haptics={false} onPress={handleQuickToggle}>
  Toggle
</EtButton>
```

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` - provides theme colors for variant styling
- `EtText` - underlying text component for `ButtonLabel`
- `EtoroIcon` - underlying icon component for `ButtonIcon`
- `ButtonContext` - React context for passing state to subcomponents

### External Dependencies

- `expo-haptics` - haptic feedback on press
- `react-native` - `Pressable`, `View`, `StyleSheet`

### Design System Integration

- Colors come from theme (`useEtoroTheme().colors`) by default, or from a fixed palette (`eToroLightColors` / `eToroDarkColors`) when `forceColorScheme` is set
- Spacing uses design tokens (`X2`, `X5`, `X9` from `core/styles/spacing`)
- Typography variants from `TextVariant` system

## Patterns & Pitfalls

### Loading state replaces content

When `loading={true}` and there's a single child, the button shows a spinner icon while preserving button width. The original content is hidden.

### Disabled blocks both press and loading

When `disabled={true}` or `loading={true}`, the button:

- Ignores `onPress` callbacks
- Shows disabled styling
- Has `accessibilityState={{ disabled: true }}`

## Related Context

- `EtText (et-text.tsx)` - EtText component used internally
- `EtoroIcon  (et-icon.tsx)` - EtoroIcon component used internally
- `EtIconButton  (et-icon-button.tsx)` - icon-only circular button. No theme color references of its own; it is a thin `Pressable` wrapper around `EtoroIcon`, so V2 color-token migration ships transitively via the foundation icon hook.
